4. Third-party quotations in the research corpus
--------------------------------------------------
`docs/research/personas/essentialist/` holds a primary-source corpus used to
distill the Essentialist persona. These files contain short excerpts and
structured notes quoted from third-party works — writings, speeches, and
interviews by Dieter Rams, Walter Gropius, Jonathan Ive, and others — for
purposes of commentary, analysis, and attribution. Each file opens with a
provenance header recording source URL, author, original date where known,
date accessed, and retrieval method. These excerpts remain the property of
their respective copyright holders and are NOT licensed under this
repository's LICENSE. They are quoted, not relicensed.

The same applies to `Figma Design/`, which holds this project's own notes
from interviewing Figma Make about its design workflow. The notes are
original work; any product behavior they describe belongs to its owner.

5. vitrea — the material runtime (`packages/`, `apps/`)
--------------------------------------------------------
`packages/` and `apps/` hold vitrea, this repository's second artifact: a
TypeScript library replicating Apple's Liquid Glass material on the web. It is
original work written from scratch for this project. Copyright (c) 2026
Minhyeok Kim, licensed under the Apache License 2.0 in LICENSE. No Apple code,
asset, or framework is included, adapted, or redistributed.

Two published npm packages come out of it -- `vitrea` and `vitrea-react` --
each shipping its own copy of LICENSE and a package-scoped NOTICE
(`packages/core/NOTICE`, `packages/react/NOTICE`) carrying the trademark
clause below. The remaining workspace packages are internal, never published,
and bundled into those two.

`apps/reference-apple/fixtures/` holds screen captures of Apple's own
rendering of its Liquid Glass material on macOS 26.5. They exist solely as
measurement ground truth -- the reference a fidelity claim is diffed against
-- and are quoted for comparison, analysis, and verification. They are not
original work, are not licensed under this repository's LICENSE, and remain
the property of their copyright holder.

